id: joint-protection
name: Joint Protection
kind: crafting
categories: armor
slots: 1
# "The first time in a Combat Encounter that your Break Value would be lowered while being at
# its maximum Break Value, your Break Value is not lowered." Read by the Break Value.
sparesFirstBreak: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Once a Combat Encounter, the first loss of Break Value from full does not happen.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: its Effects line as printed, word for
# word, cut into one line to an effect, each opening with its tag as the rulebook writes one.
summary: >
  [Automatic, 1/Encounter]: The first time in a Combat Encounter that your Break Value would be
  lowered while being at its maximum Break Value, your Break Value is not lowered.
text: >
  Joint Protection: This armor covers your joints, reducing the chances of them being injured.
  –Apparel Category: Armor
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –Quality Slots: 1
  –Effects: The first time in a Combat Encounter that your Break Value would be lowered while
  being at its maximum Break Value, your Break Value is not lowered.

---

# --- What is not built ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Losing Break Value comes with the rest of the Apparel rules. When it does: a piece with this
# on it, at its maximum Break Value, loses nothing the first time in a Combat Encounter it would,
# and that once is kept with the other once-per-Encounter uses.
